<title>POLAND: Polish consumer electronics mkt up 14 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Polish consumer electronics mkt up 14 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer electronics sales rose 14 percent last year to $1.114 billion, an independent Warsaw-based Electronic Market Institute said in a report on Thursday.</p>
<p>The institute said the sales were likely to grow by three percent to $1.152 billion in 1997 and by 10 percent in 1998 to 1.272 billion.</p>
<p>In 1996 the fastest growth, of 40 percent, was in sales of audio equipment, which contributed 28 percent or $321 million to overall electronic sales, it said. TV sets sales, which amount to 60 percent of overall sales, rose four percent.</p>
<p>SALES OF ELECTRONIC EQUIPMENT (in million of dollars)</p>
<p>			     1995	   1996	  f1997	f1998</p>
<p> TV SETS ($million)     639	    663	    636	  688</p>
<p> share of imports (pct)  17	     17	     19	   19</p>
<p> VIDEO ($million)	 110	    130	    154	  179</p>
<p> share of imports (pct)  90	     91	     91	   90</p>
<p> AUDIO ($million)	 230	    321	    362	  405</p>
<p> share of imports (pct)  85	     91	     90	   91</p>
<p> TOTAL ($million)	 979	  1.114	  1.152	1.272</p>
<p> share of imports (pct)  33	     47	     51	   51</p>
